  partName: Intake Valve (2)
  description: The Intake Valve (2) is a tiny, elongated component positioned at
    the top-center-center of the engine, constructed from Material.001, which regulates
    the flow of air and fuel into the combustion chamber. Its role is vital, as it
    enables the engine to operate efficiently, and an interesting detail is that
    it is designed to work in conjunction with the exhaust valve to ensure a balanced
    flow of gases in and out of the combustion chamber. The intake valve's material
    properties enable it to withstand the high temperatures and pressures associated
    with engine operation.
